window.META_MATH = {"subject": "Functional Analysis and Measure Theory", "projects": [{"id": "FA-01", "slug": "monotone-convergence-theorem", "title": "Monotone Convergence Theorem", "level": "Introductory", "idea": "<p>Test the limit against one simple function at a time. A factor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>\nmakes the eventual comparison with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nvalid even where the limit equals the test function.</p>", "target": "<p>On any measure space\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_n:X\\to[0,\\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe measurable with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_n\\le f_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>\neverywhere. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sup</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=\\sup_n f_n</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>f</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int f\\,d\\mu=\\lim_n\\int f_n\\,d\\mu</annotation></semantics></math>,\nallowing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">+\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.\nNo finiteness or sigma-finiteness of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu</annotation></semantics></math>\nis assumed.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use countable additivity, continuity from below for measures, and the\ndefinition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sup</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mi>s</mi><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> finite-valued measurable simple</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int h=\\sup\\{\\int s:0\\le s\\le h,\\ s\\text{ finite-valued measurable simple}\\}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor disjoint measurable\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_i</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_i\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int\\sum_i a_i1_{A_i}=\\sum_i a_i\\mu(A_i)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\cdot\\infty=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nContinuity from below follows by decomposing an increasing union into\ndisjoint successive differences. Integral monotonicity follows directly\nfrom the supremum definition.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Simple-function comparison", "role": "<p>Approximate the support of each positive level from below by places\nwhere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas reached\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">cs</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Local obligation:</strong> For every such\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lim_n\\int f_n\\ge c\\int s</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>A fixed simple\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s=\\sum_{i=1}^m a_i1_{A_i}\\le f</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith disjoint\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_i</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0&lt;c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>For every such\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lim_n\\int f_n\\ge c\\int s</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>At a point with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe strict margin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">cs&lt;s\\le f</annotation></semantics></math>\nis essential; do not claim eventual attainment of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s</annotation></semantics></math>\nitself.</p>", "repair": "<p>If a candidate uses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nrestore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0&lt;c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand repeat the support exhaustion before taking any limit. Withhold this\nexport and recheck its descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>The supremum of measurable functions is measurable, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nis measurable. Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_n=\\{x:f_n(x)\\ge c s(x)\\}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThese measurable sets increase. Every point with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s(x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in their union, since otherwise\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)\\le cs(x)&lt;s(x)</annotation></semantics></math>;\npoints with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nalready lie in every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">cs1_{B_n}\\le f_n</annotation></semantics></math>,\nmonotonicity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int f_n\\ge c\\sum_i a_i\\mu(A_i\\cap B_n)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nContinuity from below gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>↑</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu(A_i\\cap B_n)\\uparrow\\mu(A_i)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe sum has finitely many nonnegative terms, so its limit is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int s</annotation></semantics></math>,\nalso when a positive term is infinite. This proves the export.</p>"], "components": {"Contract": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: For every such\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lim_n\\int f_n\\ge c\\int s</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Knowledge": "<p>A fixed simple\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s=\\sum_{i=1}^m a_i1_{A_i}\\le f</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith disjoint\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_i</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0&lt;c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Strategy": "<p>Approximate the support of each positive level from below by places\nwhere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas reached\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">cs</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Validation": "<p>At a point with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe strict margin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">cs&lt;s\\le f</annotation></semantics></math>\nis essential; do not claim eventual attainment of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s</annotation></semantics></math>\nitself.</p>", "Execution": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Supremum and extended values", "role": "<p>Take the scalar limit\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>↑</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c\\uparrow1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen the supremum over simple functions. <strong>Local\nobligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lim_n\\int f_n=\\int f</annotation></semantics></math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[0,\\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le f_n\\le f</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe integral is defined by simple minorants. Incoming proof exports:\nE1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lim_n\\int f_n=\\int f</annotation></semantics></math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[0,\\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>Never subtract two infinite integrals; handle the extended-real\ncomparison directly.</p>", "repair": "<p>If infinity is treated as an ordinary real number, replace that\nmanipulation with the two order inequalities just proved. Withhold this\nexport and recheck its descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Put\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=\\lim_n\\int f_n</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhich exists in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[0,\\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>\nbecause the integrals increase. E1 gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L\\ge c\\int s</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int s&lt;\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>↑</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c\\uparrow1</annotation></semantics></math>\nto obtain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L\\ge\\int s</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int s=\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,\nany fixed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nalready gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Taking the supremum over all simple\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s\\le f</annotation></semantics></math>\nyields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L\\ge\\int f</annotation></semantics></math>.\nConversely\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_n\\le f</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int f_n\\le\\int f</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≤</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L\\le\\int f</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe two comparisons prove the asserted equality without an infinity\nsubtraction.</p>"], "components": {"Contract": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lim_n\\int f_n=\\int f</annotation></semantics></math>\nin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[0,\\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Knowledge": "<p>E1/v1 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le f_n\\le f</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe integral is defined by simple minorants. Incoming proof exports:\nE1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Strategy": "<p>Take the scalar limit\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>↑</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c\\uparrow1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen the supremum over simple functions.</p>", "Validation": "<p>Never subtract two infinite integrals; handle the extended-real\ncomparison directly.</p>", "Execution": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le f_n\\le f</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe integral is defined by simple minorants. Check: Never subtract two\ninfinite integrals; handle the extended-real comparison directly.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-simple-function-comparison-1\">N1 — Simple-function\ncomparison</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> The supremum of measurable functions is\nmeasurable, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nis measurable. Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_n=\\{x:f_n(x)\\ge c s(x)\\}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThese measurable sets increase. Every point with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s(x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in their union, since otherwise\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)\\le cs(x)&lt;s(x)</annotation></semantics></math>;\npoints with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nalready lie in every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> Because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">cs1_{B_n}\\le f_n</annotation></semantics></math>,\nmonotonicity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int f_n\\ge c\\sum_i a_i\\mu(A_i\\cap B_n)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nContinuity from below gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>↑</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mu(A_i\\cap B_n)\\uparrow\\mu(A_i)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe sum has finitely many nonnegative terms, so its limit is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int s</annotation></semantics></math>,\nalso when a positive term is infinite. This proves the export.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-supremum-and-extended-values-1\">N2 — Supremum and extended\nvalues</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> Put\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=\\lim_n\\int f_n</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhich exists in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[0,\\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>\nbecause the integrals increase. E1 gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L\\ge c\\int s</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int s&lt;\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>↑</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c\\uparrow1</annotation></semantics></math>\nto obtain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L\\ge\\int s</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int s=\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,\nany fixed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nalready gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> Taking the supremum over all simple\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s\\le f</annotation></semantics></math>\nyields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L\\ge\\int f</annotation></semantics></math>.\nConversely\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_n\\le f</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int f_n\\le\\int f</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≤</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L\\le\\int f</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe two comparisons prove the asserted equality without an infinity\nsubtraction.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For Lebesgue measure on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntake\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_n(x)=\\min(n,1/x)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIt increases to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/x</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSplitting at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/n</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_0^1 f_n=1+\\log n</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence the theorem correctly returns\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\int_0^1 dx/x=\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis exercises the extended-valued conclusion.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>On\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_n=n1_{(0,1/n)}</annotation></semantics></math>\ntends pointwise to zero but has integral one. The sequence is not\nincreasing; pointwise convergence alone cannot replace the monotonicity\nhypothesis.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected candidate (N1.1):</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s\\le f</annotation></semantics></math>\nimplies eventually\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s\\le f_n</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTake\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s=f=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_n=1-1/(n+1)</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Strategy lost the strict comparison margin.\n<strong>Repair:</strong> compare\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">cs</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen use N2 to pass\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>↑</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c\\uparrow1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis fills the proof under the original hypotheses. Recheck E1 and E2;\nthe target is unchanged.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Use this export to prove Fatou’s lemma by applying\nit to the increasing tail infima of a nonnegative sequence.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-102-introduction-to-functional-analysis-spring-2021/resources/lecture-notes/\">MIT\nOpenCourseWare, Introduction to Functional Analysis: lecture notes</a>.\nSee the lectures on integration, Hilbert spaces, Baire category, and\nHahn–Banach.</p>", "sha256": "b277eb0c4a5f68b968d5e4ee310c7efce992311b000d6ec1aa03a8bc676ea263", "pdf": "reports/pdf/monotone-convergence-theorem.pdf"}, {"id": "FA-02", "slug": "hilbert-projection-theorem", "title": "Hilbert Projection Theorem", "level": "Intermediate", "idea": "<p>A minimizing sequence need not converge merely because its distances\nconverge. The parallelogram identity converts near-minimality into the\nmissing Cauchy estimate.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe a real or complex Hilbert space and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M\\subset H</annotation></semantics></math>\na closed linear subspace. For each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>\nthere exists a unique\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>\nminimizing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x-m\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nMoreover\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x-m\\perp M</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand the map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_Mx=m</annotation></semantics></math>\nis linear with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|P_Mx\\|\\le\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nInner products are linear in the first variable.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use completeness of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe parallelogram identity, Cauchy–Schwarz, and the polarization rules\nfor a complex inner product. A closed subspace contains limits of its\nconvergent sequences. The infimum property supplies a sequence\napproaching a finite infimum.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Attain the distance", "role": "<p>Use the midpoint in the subspace to control differences of two\nminimizing terms. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> There is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x-m\\|=d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">inf</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=\\inf_{m\\in M}\\|x-m\\|</annotation></semantics></math>\nand a sequence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m_n\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x-m_n\\|\\to d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>There is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x-m\\|=d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The midpoint lies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>;\ncompleteness gives a limit in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H</annotation></semantics></math>\nand closedness places it in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the minimizing sequence is declared convergent without an\nestimate, insert the parallelogram bound; if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>\nis not closed, the original attainment claim needs a changed hypothesis.\nWithhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le d\\le\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nChoose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x-m_n\\|&lt;d+1/n</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe parallelogram identity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|m_n-m_k\\|^2=2\\|x-m_n\\|^2+2\\|x-m_k\\|^2-4\\|x-(m_n+m_k)/2\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe final squared norm is at least\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d^2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The resulting upper bound tends to zero as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n,k\\to\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(m_n)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis Cauchy and converges in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H</annotation></semantics></math>\nto some\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nClosedness gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand continuity of the norm gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x-m\\|=d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "components": {"Contract": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: There is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x-m\\|=d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Knowledge": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">inf</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=\\inf_{m\\in M}\\|x-m\\|</annotation></semantics></math>\nand a sequence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m_n\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x-m_n\\|\\to d</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Strategy": "<p>Use the midpoint in the subspace to control differences of two\nminimizing terms.</p>", "Validation": "<p>The midpoint lies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>;\ncompleteness gives a limit in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H</annotation></semantics></math>\nand closedness places it in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Execution": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Orthogonality and uniqueness", "role": "<p>Vary the minimizer along real and imaginary scalar multiples of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x-m\\perp M</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand this condition characterizes the unique minimizer.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1, a minimizer\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x-m\\perp M</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand this condition characterizes the unique minimizer.</p>", "gate": "<p>In a complex space, real variations alone only eliminate the real\npart of the inner product.</p>", "repair": "<p>If only real orthogonality has been checked, add the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">iv</annotation></semantics></math>\nvariation and revalidate uniqueness. Withhold this export and recheck\nits descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=x-m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor real\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>,\nminimality implies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>v</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Re</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le\\|r-tv\\|^2-\\|r\\|^2=-2t\\operatorname{Re}\\langle r,v\\rangle+t^2\\|v\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTaking small positive and negative\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>\nforces\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Re</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Re}\\langle r,v\\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIn the complex case repeat with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">iv</annotation></semantics></math>\nto get the imaginary part zero.</p>", "<p>For any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>,\northogonality gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>+</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x-w\\|^2=\\|r\\|^2+\\|m-w\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nHence equality with the minimum holds only for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w=m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nConversely an orthogonal residual gives this identity and therefore a\nminimizer.</p>"], "components": {"Contract": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x-m\\perp M</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand this condition characterizes the unique minimizer.</p>", "Knowledge": "<p>E1/v1, a minimizer\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Strategy": "<p>Vary the minimizer along real and imaginary scalar multiples of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Validation": "<p>In a complex space, real variations alone only eliminate the real\npart of the inner product.</p>", "Execution": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N3", "title": "The projection operator", "role": "<p>Apply uniqueness of the orthogonal decomposition to sums and scalar\nmultiples. <strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_M</annotation></semantics></math>\nis linear and contractive:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|P_Mx\\|\\le\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E2/v1 for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E2/v1 at N3.1.</p>", "exportId": "E3", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_M</annotation></semantics></math>\nis linear and contractive:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|P_Mx\\|\\le\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The argument uses that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a linear subspace, not merely a closed set.</p>", "repair": "<p>If projection onto a nonlinear closed set is claimed linear, restore\nthe subspace contract; linearity is not part of the general convex\nprojection theorem. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants\nafter a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x,y\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>\nand scalars\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a,b</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">aP_Mx+bP_My</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhile\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a(x-P_Mx)+b(y-P_My)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis orthogonal to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>.\nE2 identifies this as the unique decomposition of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ax+by</annotation></semantics></math>,\nproving linearity.</p>", "<p>The decomposition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=P_Mx+(x-P_Mx)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis orthogonal, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>+</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x\\|^2=\\|P_Mx\\|^2+\\|x-P_Mx\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis proves the norm bound and completes all assertions.</p>"], "components": {"Contract": "<p>Publish E3/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P_M</annotation></semantics></math>\nis linear and contractive:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|P_Mx\\|\\le\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Knowledge": "<p>E2/v1 for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E2/v1 at N3.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Strategy": "<p>Apply uniqueness of the orthogonal decomposition to sums and scalar\nmultiples.</p>", "Validation": "<p>The argument uses that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a linear subspace, not merely a closed set.</p>", "Execution": "<p>Carry out activities N3.1–N3.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1, a minimizer\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: In a complex space, real variations alone only eliminate the real\npart of the inner product.</p>"}, {"id": "T2-3", "source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "activity": "N3.1", "gate": "<p>E2/v1 for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: The argument uses that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a linear subspace, not merely a closed set.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-attain-the-distance-1\">N1 — Attain the distance</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le d\\le\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nChoose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x-m_n\\|&lt;d+1/n</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe parallelogram identity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|m_n-m_k\\|^2=2\\|x-m_n\\|^2+2\\|x-m_k\\|^2-4\\|x-(m_n+m_k)/2\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe final squared norm is at least\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d^2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> The resulting upper bound tends to zero as\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n,k\\to\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(m_n)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis Cauchy and converges in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H</annotation></semantics></math>\nto some\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nClosedness gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand continuity of the norm gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x-m\\|=d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-orthogonality-and-uniqueness-1\">N2 — Orthogonality and\nuniqueness</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> Write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=x-m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor real\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>,\nminimality implies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>v</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>−</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Re</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le\\|r-tv\\|^2-\\|r\\|^2=-2t\\operatorname{Re}\\langle r,v\\rangle+t^2\\|v\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTaking small positive and negative\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>\nforces\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Re</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Re}\\langle r,v\\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIn the complex case repeat with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">iv</annotation></semantics></math>\nto get the imaginary part zero.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> For any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w\\in M</annotation></semantics></math>,\northogonality gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>+</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x-w\\|^2=\\|r\\|^2+\\|m-w\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nHence equality with the minimum holds only for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w=m</annotation></semantics></math>.\nConversely an orthogonal residual gives this identity and therefore a\nminimizer.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-the-projection-operator-1\">N3 — The projection operator</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N3.1.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x,y\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>\nand scalars\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a,b</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">aP_Mx+bP_My</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhile\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a(x-P_Mx)+b(y-P_My)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis orthogonal to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>.\nE2 identifies this as the unique decomposition of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">ax+by</annotation></semantics></math>,\nproving linearity.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N3.2.</strong> The decomposition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=P_Mx+(x-P_Mx)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis orthogonal, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>+</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|x\\|^2=\\|P_Mx\\|^2+\\|x-P_Mx\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis proves the norm bound and completes all assertions.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>In\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R^3</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>:</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M=\\{(a,b,0):a,b\\in\\mathbb R\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=(2,-1,3)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe candidate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=(2,-1,0)</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas residual\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(0,0,3)</annotation></semantics></math>\nperpendicular to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(a,b,0)</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe squared distance is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">9+(2-a)^2+(-1-b)^2</annotation></semantics></math>,\ncertifying the unique minimizer and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H=\\ell^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>00</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M=c_{00}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe finitely supported sequences. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>n</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=(1/n)_{n\\ge1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntruncations in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>\napproach\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso the infimum distance is zero. It is not attained because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\notin M</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis isolates closedness.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected export (N1):</strong> every subspace admits a\nclosest point. <strong>Validation witness:</strong> the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c_{00}</annotation></semantics></math>\nexample above. <strong>Knowledge diagnosis:</strong> closedness was dropped\nwhen moving from a limit in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H</annotation></semantics></math>\nto membership in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Repair:</strong> keep the stated closed-subspace hypothesis and\nexplicitly invoke it in N1.2. This repairs the proof of the stated\ntheorem; extending it to all subspaces is false. N2 and N3 must consume\nthe corrected membership export.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Construct orthogonal decompositions and then the\nHilbert-space representation of continuous linear functionals in\nFA-03.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-102-introduction-to-functional-analysis-spring-2021/resources/lecture-notes/\">MIT\nOpenCourseWare, Introduction to Functional Analysis: lecture notes</a>.\nSee the lectures on integration, Hilbert spaces, Baire category, and\nHahn–Banach.</p>", "sha256": "26bb081f6139ffc88aee6bf5fc3dadc86c44063c54e6b6ef9ae67f0616abe533", "pdf": "reports/pdf/hilbert-projection-theorem.pdf"}, {"id": "FA-03", "slug": "riesz-representation-hilbert-spaces", "title": "Riesz Representation in Hilbert Spaces", "level": "Intermediate", "idea": "<p>The kernel has an orthogonal direction that captures every value of\nthe functional; scaling that direction gives the representing\nvector.</p>", "target": "<p>For a real or complex Hilbert space\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith inner product linear in its first variable, every bounded linear\nfunctional\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell:H\\to\\mathbb F</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas a unique\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>\nsuch that\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(x)=\\langle x,y\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAlso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|\\ell\\|=\\|y\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Import FA-02: every vector has a unique orthogonal decomposition\nrelative to a closed linear subspace. Use Cauchy–Schwarz and continuity\nof bounded linear maps. The operator norm is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sup</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|\\ell\\|=\\sup_{\\|x\\|\\le1}|\\ell(x)|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThis is the Hilbert-space Riesz theorem, not the measure representation\ntheorem on spaces of continuous functions.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Separate the kernel", "role": "<p>Project a vector outside the kernel and retain its nonzero\nperpendicular remainder. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> There is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\in K^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(z)\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>z</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x-\\ell(x)z/\\ell(z)\\in K</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>A nonzero bounded functional\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℓ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell</annotation></semantics></math>;\nits kernel\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>There is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\in K^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(z)\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>z</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x-\\ell(x)z/\\ell(z)\\in K</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The remainder cannot vanish or lie in the kernel, because its\nfunctional value equals the original nonzero value.</p>", "repair": "<p>If division by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(z)</annotation></semantics></math>\noccurs before nonvanishing is shown, restore the separate\nzero-functional case and the equality\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(z)=\\ell(w)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWithhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntake\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the representation and norm equality are immediate; uniqueness\nfollows from testing the difference against itself as in N2. For the\nremaining case choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(w)\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nContinuity makes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\nclosed, so FA-02 gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w=P_Kw+z</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\perp K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Linearity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(z)=\\ell(w)\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>,\nset\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>z</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=x-\\ell(x)z/\\ell(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(k)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k\\in K</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle x,z\\rangle=\\ell(x)\\|z\\|^2/\\ell(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "components": {"Contract": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: There is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\in K^\\perp</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(z)\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>z</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x-\\ell(x)z/\\ell(z)\\in K</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Knowledge": "<p>A nonzero bounded functional\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℓ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell</annotation></semantics></math>;\nits kernel\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Strategy": "<p>Project a vector outside the kernel and retain its nonzero\nperpendicular remainder.</p>", "Validation": "<p>The remainder cannot vanish or lie in the kernel, because its\nfunctional value equals the original nonzero value.</p>", "Execution": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Normalize and certify the norm", "role": "<p>Choose the conjugate scalar in the second argument, then test at the\nnormalized representing vector. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> A\nunique\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y</annotation></semantics></math>\nrepresents\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℓ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|\\ell\\|=\\|y\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1; the first-variable linear convention. Incoming proof exports:\nE1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p>A unique\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y</annotation></semantics></math>\nrepresents\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℓ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|\\ell\\|=\\|y\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The scalar in the second inner-product argument is conjugated;\nomitting it changes the represented functional over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "repair": "<p>If conjugation is absent, recompute the second-argument scalar and\ncheck the one-dimensional complex example before releasing the norm and\nrepresentation. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after a\nversioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mover><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover><mi>z</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=\\overline{\\ell(z)}z/\\|z\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>\n(drop conjugation over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>).\nThen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle x,y\\rangle=\\ell(z)\\langle x,z\\rangle/\\|z\\|^2=\\ell(x)</annotation></semantics></math>\nby E1.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y_1,y_2</annotation></semantics></math>\nrepresent the same functional,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle x,y_1-y_2\\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTaking\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=y_1-y_2</annotation></semantics></math>\nproves equality. Cauchy–Schwarz gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|\\ell\\|\\le\\|y\\|</annotation></semantics></math>;\nif\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntesting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=y/\\|y\\|</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives the reverse inequality. The zero case has both norms zero.</p>"], "components": {"Contract": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation: A unique\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y</annotation></semantics></math>\nrepresents\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℓ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|\\ell\\|=\\|y\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Knowledge": "<p>E1/v1; the first-variable linear convention. Incoming proof exports:\nE1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Strategy": "<p>Choose the conjugate scalar in the second argument, then test at the\nnormalized representing vector.</p>", "Validation": "<p>The scalar in the second inner-product argument is conjugated;\nomitting it changes the represented functional over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Execution": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1; the first-variable linear convention. Check: The scalar in the\nsecond inner-product argument is conjugated; omitting it changes the\nrepresented functional over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-separate-the-kernel-1\">N1 — Separate the kernel</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntake\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the representation and norm equality are immediate; uniqueness\nfollows from testing the difference against itself as in N2. For the\nremaining case choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(w)\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nContinuity makes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K</annotation></semantics></math>\nclosed, so FA-02 gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w=P_Kw+z</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\perp K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> Linearity gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(z)=\\ell(w)\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>,\nset\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>z</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k=x-\\ell(x)z/\\ell(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(k)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k\\in K</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle x,z\\rangle=\\ell(x)\\|z\\|^2/\\ell(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-normalize-and-certify-the-norm-1\">N2 — Normalize and certify\nthe norm</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> Define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mover><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover><mi>z</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=\\overline{\\ell(z)}z/\\|z\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>\n(drop conjugation over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>).\nThen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle x,y\\rangle=\\ell(z)\\langle x,z\\rangle/\\|z\\|^2=\\ell(x)</annotation></semantics></math>\nby E1.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y_1,y_2</annotation></semantics></math>\nrepresent the same functional,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle x,y_1-y_2\\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTaking\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=y_1-y_2</annotation></semantics></math>\nproves equality. Cauchy–Schwarz gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|\\ell\\|\\le\\|y\\|</annotation></semantics></math>;\nif\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\ne0</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntesting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=y/\\|y\\|</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives the reverse inequality. The zero case has both norms\nzero.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>On\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb C^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mover><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo accent=\"true\">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle x,y\\rangle=x_1\\overline{y_1}+x_2\\overline{y_2}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(x)=x_1+2i x_2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts representing vector is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=(1,-2i)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|\\ell\\|=\\sqrt5</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe unit vector\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>/</mi><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y/\\sqrt5</annotation></semantics></math>\nattains the operator norm. This checks the conjugation convention\ndirectly.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Completeness matters: on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c_{00}</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nnorm,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>/</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(x)=\\sum_n x_n/n</annotation></semantics></math>\nis bounded by Cauchy–Schwarz. A representing vector within\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c_{00}</annotation></semantics></math>\nwould have coordinates\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/n</annotation></semantics></math>\nby testing the standard basis, an impossibility. The completion\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nsupplies that vector.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N2 candidate:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>z</mi><mi>/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=\\ell(z)z/\\|z\\|^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nunder the first-variable linear convention. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H=\\mathbb C</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(x)=ix</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nit gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⟩</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle x,i\\rangle=-ix</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Knowledge used the wrong scalar convention.\n<strong>Repair:</strong> conjugate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell(z)</annotation></semantics></math>\nas in N2.1. The statement is unchanged; recheck both the representation\nand its norm certificate.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Apply the representation to bounded variational\nfunctionals, as in the weak Poisson existence project.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-102-introduction-to-functional-analysis-spring-2021/resources/lecture-notes/\">MIT\nOpenCourseWare, Introduction to Functional Analysis: lecture notes</a>.\nSee the lectures on integration, Hilbert spaces, Baire category, and\nHahn–Banach.</p>", "sha256": "06937a6f1c206cceef839f875cd90b9d8f24620a45ee3ba3ac8ac27d8528b78a", "pdf": "reports/pdf/riesz-representation-hilbert-spaces.pdf"}, {"id": "FA-04", "slug": "uniform-boundedness-principle", "title": "Uniform Boundedness Principle", "level": "Intermediate", "idea": "<p>Convert bounds depending on the point into one common bound on a\nball, then subtract its center and rescale.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe a Banach space,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>\na normed space, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝒯</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal T</annotation></semantics></math>\na family of bounded linear maps\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X\\to Y</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf for every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\in X</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe number\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sup</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sup_{T\\in\\mathcal T}\\|Tx\\|</annotation></semantics></math>\nis finite, prove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sup</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sup_{T\\in\\mathcal T}\\|T\\|&lt;\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe family need not be countable, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>\nneed not be complete.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Import the Baire category theorem: a nonempty complete metric space\ncannot be a countable union of closed sets with empty interior. Use\ncontinuity of bounded operators, the triangle inequality, and the\noperator norm. The empty family satisfies the boundedness conclusion\nvacuously; treat the nonempty case below.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Find a uniformly controlled ball", "role": "<p>Apply Baire to the countable collection of level sets, even when the\noperator family is uncountable. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> There\nare\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B(x_0,r)\\subset F_N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sup</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_n=\\{x:\\sup_{T\\in\\mathcal T}\\|Tx\\|\\le n\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor integers\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p>There are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B(x_0,r)\\subset F_N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>Each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an arbitrary intersection of closed inverse images; countability is\nneeded for the cover by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_n</annotation></semantics></math>,\nnot for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝒯</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "repair": "<p>If Baire is applied to the operator index set, rebuild the countable\nlevel-set cover of the complete space\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWithhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\{x:\\|Tx\\|\\le n\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis closed by continuity, so their intersection\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nis closed. Pointwise boundedness says\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X=\\bigcup_{n\\ge1}F_n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The Banach space\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a nonempty complete metric space. Baire therefore gives an\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_N</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith nonempty interior, which contains some open ball\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B(x_0,r)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIn particular\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0\\in F_N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "components": {"Contract": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation: There are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B(x_0,r)\\subset F_N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Knowledge": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sup</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_n=\\{x:\\sup_{T\\in\\mathcal T}\\|Tx\\|\\le n\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor integers\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\ge1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Strategy": "<p>Apply Baire to the countable collection of level sets, even when the\noperator family is uncountable.</p>", "Validation": "<p>Each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nis an arbitrary intersection of closed inverse images; countability is\nneeded for the cover by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_n</annotation></semantics></math>,\nnot for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>𝒯</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Execution": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Center and rescale", "role": "<p>Use a difference of two points in the controlled ball to bound the\nunit ball. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> For every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T\\in\\mathcal T</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|T\\|\\le4N/r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and linearity of every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p>For every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T\\in\\mathcal T</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|T\\|\\le4N/r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>The ball is not necessarily centered at zero, so its center must be\nsubtracted before scaling.</p>", "repair": "<p>If a candidate rescales\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0+h</annotation></semantics></math>\ndirectly, replace it by the difference\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math>\nfirst; retain the factor two from the triangle inequality. Withhold this\nexport and recheck its descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|h\\|&lt;r</annotation></semantics></math>,\nboth\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0+h</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nbelong to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_N</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>+</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|Th\\|\\le\\|T(x_0+h)\\|+\\|Tx_0\\|\\le2N</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|u\\|\\le1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nchoose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=(r/2)u</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|Tu\\|=(2/r)\\|Th\\|\\le4N/r</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTaking the supremum over the unit ball and then the family proves the\ntheorem. Completeness of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>\nwas never used.</p>"], "components": {"Contract": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation: For every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T\\in\\mathcal T</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|T\\|\\le4N/r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Knowledge": "<p>E1/v1 and linearity of every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Strategy": "<p>Use a difference of two points in the controlled ball to bound the\nunit ball.</p>", "Validation": "<p>The ball is not necessarily centered at zero, so its center must be\nsubtracted before scaling.</p>", "Execution": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.1", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and linearity of every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: The ball is not necessarily centered at zero, so its center must\nbe subtracted before scaling.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-find-a-uniformly-controlled-ball-1\">N1 — Find a uniformly\ncontrolled ball</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> For each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\{x:\\|Tx\\|\\le n\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis closed by continuity, so their intersection\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nis closed. Pointwise boundedness says\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X=\\bigcup_{n\\ge1}F_n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> The Banach space\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nis a nonempty complete metric space. Baire therefore gives an\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_N</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith nonempty interior, which contains some open ball\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B(x_0,r)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIn particular\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0\\in F_N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-center-and-rescale-1\">N2 — Center and rescale</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|h\\|&lt;r</annotation></semantics></math>,\nboth\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0+h</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_0</annotation></semantics></math>\nbelong to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_N</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>+</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|Th\\|\\le\\|T(x_0+h)\\|+\\|Tx_0\\|\\le2N</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|u\\|\\le1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nchoose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=(r/2)u</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|Tu\\|=(2/r)\\|Th\\|\\le4N/r</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTaking the supremum over the unit ball and then the family proves the\ntheorem. Completeness of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math>\nwas never used.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>On\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell^2</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntake\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_nx=x_n</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor each\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sup</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sup_n|x_n|\\le\\|x\\|_2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTesting the standard basis gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|T_n\\|=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso the pointwise and uniform bounds agree. The theorem also applies when\na direct formula for the common norm bound is unavailable.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>On the incomplete normed space\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c_{00}</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith the sup norm, set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_nx=n x_n</annotation></semantics></math>.\nEach\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nis bounded with norm\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor each finitely supported\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>,\nonly finitely many\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_nx</annotation></semantics></math>\nare nonzero, so pointwise boundedness holds while uniform boundedness\nfails.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected generalization (N1.2):</strong> the theorem works\nfor every normed domain. <strong>Validation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c_{00}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_nx=nx_n</annotation></semantics></math>\nrefute it. <strong>Diagnosis:</strong> the Baire import requires\ncompleteness. <strong>Repair:</strong> retain the original Banach-domain\ncontract and apply Baire exactly there; extending the target to\narbitrary normed spaces would require new assumptions. N2 may consume\nonly the ball export proved under completeness.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Combine this with pointwise convergence of bounded\noperators to control their norms; convergence in operator norm still\nrequires additional hypotheses.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-102-introduction-to-functional-analysis-spring-2021/resources/lecture-notes/\">MIT\nOpenCourseWare, Introduction to Functional Analysis: lecture notes</a>.\nSee the lectures on integration, Hilbert spaces, Baire category, and\nHahn–Banach.</p>", "sha256": "cdf4f8a619b643d3575ce35c9cab0ec64ae2a1ad516a9f55717ed3e70dce96e7", "pdf": "reports/pdf/uniform-boundedness-principle.pdf"}, {"id": "FA-05", "slug": "hahn-banach-real-extension", "title": "Hahn–Banach Norm-Preserving Extension", "level": "Advanced", "idea": "<p>The key finite step extends a dominated functional by one direction.\nA chain-union argument then extends it to the entire space without\nclaiming countably many directions suffice.</p>", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe a real normed space,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M\\subset X</annotation></semantics></math>\nany linear subspace, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:M\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>\nbounded linear. There exists bounded linear\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:X\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F|_M=f</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|F\\|=\\|f\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nNeither completeness of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math>\nnor closedness of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>\nis assumed.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Work in set theory with Zorn’s lemma: a nonempty partially ordered\nset in which every chain has an upper bound has a maximal element. Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=\\|f\\|</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p(x)=C\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>,\na finite-valued sublinear function:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p(x+y)\\le p(x)+p(y)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p(tx)=tp(x)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t\\ge0</annotation></semantics></math>.\nUse completeness of the real order to select a number between a bounded\nsupremum and infimum.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "One-dimensional extension interval", "role": "<p>Turn domination of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(d)+ta</annotation></semantics></math>\ninto compatible lower and upper bounds for the new value\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=G(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g</annotation></semantics></math>\nextends linearly to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D+\\mathbb Rz</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhile remaining dominated by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>A linear\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g:D\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\le p</annotation></semantics></math>\non a subspace\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\notin D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "exportId": "E1", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g</annotation></semantics></math>\nextends linearly to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D+\\mathbb Rz</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhile remaining dominated by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>Both signs of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>\nmust be checked, and the choice interval must be nonempty and\nfinite.</p>", "repair": "<p>If only positive scalars were considered, restore the lower endpoint\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the negative-scalar calculation before extending the domain.\nWithhold this export and recheck its descendants after a versioned\ncorrection.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u,v\\in D</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlinearity and domination give\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(u)+g(v)=g(u+v)\\le p(u+v)\\le p(u-z)+p(v+z)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTherefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(u)-p(u-z)\\le p(v+z)-g(v)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sup</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=\\sup_u[g(u)-p(u-z)]</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">inf</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=\\inf_v[p(v+z)-g(v)]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe preceding inequality gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L\\le U</annotation></semantics></math>;\nchoosing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nbounds both endpoints between finite numbers.</p>", "<p>Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in[L,U]</annotation></semantics></math>\nand define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(d+tz)=g(d)+ta</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe representation is unique because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\notin D</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>\nis well defined and linear. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\le p(d/t+z)-g(d/t)</annotation></semantics></math>\nimplies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(d+tz)\\le p(d+tz)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=-s&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\ge g(d/s)-p(d/s-z)</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(d)-sa\\le s p(d/s-z)=p(d-sz)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe case\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nuses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\le p</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus domination holds for every real scalar.</p>"], "components": {"Contract": "<p>Publish E1/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g</annotation></semantics></math>\nextends linearly to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D+\\mathbb Rz</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhile remaining dominated by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Knowledge": "<p>A linear\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g:D\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\le p</annotation></semantics></math>\non a subspace\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\notin D</annotation></semantics></math>.\nRetain the stated assumptions and import versions.</p>", "Strategy": "<p>Turn domination of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(d)+ta</annotation></semantics></math>\ninto compatible lower and upper bounds for the new value\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=G(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Validation": "<p>Both signs of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math>\nmust be checked, and the choice interval must be nonempty and\nfinite.</p>", "Execution": "<p>Carry out activities N1.1–N1.3 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Maximal dominated extension", "role": "<p>Order compatible extensions by domain inclusion and take unions along\nchains. <strong>Local obligation:</strong> There is a linear\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:X\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>\nextending\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F\\le p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E1/v1 and all extensions of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\ndominated by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.2.</p>", "exportId": "E2", "export": "<p>There is a linear\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:X\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>\nextending\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F\\le p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>A union is a function only because the extensions agree on overlaps;\na maximal proper domain can still be extended by E1.</p>", "repair": "<p>If a union of incomparable extensions is used, restrict to chains\nbefore invoking Zorn; arbitrary extensions can assign conflicting\nvalues. Withhold this export and recheck its descendants after a\nversioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>The set of pairs\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(D,g)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M\\subset D\\subset X</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g|_M=f</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\le p</annotation></semantics></math>\nis nonempty. Order it by extension. For a chain, the union of its\ndomains is a subspace: any two vectors and their values occur together\nin one chain member. The union map is consequently well defined, linear,\nand dominated by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>This union is an upper bound, so Zorn supplies a maximal pair\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(D,g)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\ne X</annotation></semantics></math>,\nchoose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>\\</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\in X\\setminus D</annotation></semantics></math>\nand apply E1, contradicting maximality. Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D=X</annotation></semantics></math>;\ndenote the resulting map by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "components": {"Contract": "<p>Publish E2/v1 only after establishing this obligation: There is a\nlinear\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F:X\\to\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>\nextending\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F\\le p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Knowledge": "<p>E1/v1 and all extensions of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\ndominated by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E1/v1 at N2.2. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Strategy": "<p>Order compatible extensions by domain inclusion and take unions along\nchains.</p>", "Validation": "<p>A union is a function only because the extensions agree on overlaps;\na maximal proper domain can still be extended by E1.</p>", "Execution": "<p>Carry out activities N2.1–N2.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Recover the norm equality", "role": "<p>Apply the one-sided domination to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-x</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen compare with the restriction. <strong>Local obligation:</strong>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F|_M=f</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|F\\|=\\|f\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>E2/v1 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p(x)=C\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E2/v1 at N3.1.</p>", "exportId": "E3", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F|_M=f</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|F\\|=\\|f\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "gate": "<p>One-sided domination alone must be converted to an absolute bound;\nthe zero-functional case is included.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the norm conclusion is inferred directly from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F\\le p</annotation></semantics></math>,\nadd the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-x</annotation></semantics></math>\nbound and the restriction inequality. Withhold this export and recheck\nits descendants after a versioned correction.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x)\\le C\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-F(x)=F(-x)\\le C\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nHence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|F(x)|\\le C\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math>\nis bounded and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|F\\|\\le C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Restricting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math>\nto the unit ball of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|f\\|\\le\\|F\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=\\|f\\|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nequality follows. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthis argument yields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand still applies.</p>"], "components": {"Contract": "<p>Publish E3/v1 only after establishing this obligation:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F|_M=f</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|F\\|=\\|f\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Knowledge": "<p>E2/v1 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p(x)=C\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIncoming proof exports: E2/v1 at N3.1. Retain the stated assumptions and\nimport versions.</p>", "Strategy": "<p>Apply the one-sided domination to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-x</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen compare with the restriction.</p>", "Validation": "<p>One-sided domination alone must be converted to an absolute bound;\nthe zero-functional case is included.</p>", "Execution": "<p>Carry out activities N3.1–N3.2 below, retaining each calculation and\nconstruction as evidence.</p>"}}], "edges": [{"id": "T1-2", "source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "activity": "N2.2", "gate": "<p>E1/v1 and all extensions of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\ndominated by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: A union is a function only because the extensions agree on\noverlaps; a maximal proper domain can still be extended by E1.</p>"}, {"id": "T2-3", "source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "activity": "N3.1", "gate": "<p>E2/v1 and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p(x)=C\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nCheck: One-sided domination alone must be converted to an absolute\nbound; the zero-functional case is included.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-one-dimensional-extension-interval-1\">N1 — One-dimensional\nextension interval</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N1.1.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u,v\\in D</annotation></semantics></math>,\nlinearity and domination give\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(u)+g(v)=g(u+v)\\le p(u+v)\\le p(u-z)+p(v+z)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTherefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(u)-p(u-z)\\le p(v+z)-g(v)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSet\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sup</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=\\sup_u[g(u)-p(u-z)]</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">inf</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=\\inf_v[p(v+z)-g(v)]</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe preceding inequality gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L\\le U</annotation></semantics></math>;\nchoosing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nbounds both endpoints between finite numbers.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.2.</strong> Choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in[L,U]</annotation></semantics></math>\nand define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(d+tz)=g(d)+ta</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe representation is unique because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\notin D</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>\nis well defined and linear. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\le p(d/t+z)-g(d/t)</annotation></semantics></math>\nimplies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(d+tz)\\le p(d+tz)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N1.3.</strong> For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=-s&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\ge g(d/s)-p(d/s-z)</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(d)-sa\\le s p(d/s-z)=p(d-sz)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe case\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nuses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\le p</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus domination holds for every real scalar.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-maximal-dominated-extension-1\">N2 — Maximal dominated\nextension</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N2.1.</strong> The set of pairs\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(D,g)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M\\subset D\\subset X</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g|_M=f</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\le p</annotation></semantics></math>\nis nonempty. Order it by extension. For a chain, the union of its\ndomains is a subspace: any two vectors and their values occur together\nin one chain member. The union map is consequently well defined, linear,\nand dominated by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N2.2.</strong> This union is an upper bound, so Zorn\nsupplies a maximal pair\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(D,g)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D\\ne X</annotation></semantics></math>,\nchoose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>\\</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z\\in X\\setminus D</annotation></semantics></math>\nand apply E1, contradicting maximality. Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D=X</annotation></semantics></math>;\ndenote the resulting map by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-recover-the-norm-equality-1\">N3 — Recover the norm\nequality</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>N3.1.</strong> For every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x)\\le C\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-F(x)=F(-x)\\le C\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nHence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|F(x)|\\le C\\|x\\|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math>\nis bounded and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|F\\|\\le C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>N3.2.</strong> Restricting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math>\nto the unit ball of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|f\\|\\le\\|F\\|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=\\|f\\|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nequality follows. If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C=0</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthis argument yields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F=0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand still applies.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>In\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith the Euclidean norm, take\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M=\\{(t,t)\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(t,t)=2t</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe norm on\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe extension\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(x,y)=x+y</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas norm\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand restricts correctly. This is a concrete certificate; the general\nconstruction does not promise a unique extension.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>Uniqueness is false. In\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb R^2</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell^1</annotation></semantics></math>\nnorm, let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the first coordinate axis and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x,0)=x</annotation></semantics></math>.\nEvery\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_a(x,y)=x+ay</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|a|\\le1</annotation></semantics></math>\nextends\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math>\nand has norm one.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Rejected argument, diagnosis, and correction", "html": "<p><strong>Rejected N1 candidate:</strong> choose any\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a</annotation></semantics></math>\nbelow the upper bound and ignore the lower bound. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X=\\mathbb R</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D=\\{0\\}</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p(t)=|t|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nchoosing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=-2</annotation></semantics></math>\nsatisfies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\le1</annotation></semantics></math>\nbut fails domination at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwhere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(-1)=2&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.\n<strong>Repair:</strong> require\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a\\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe actual two-sided interval. This corrects the extension argument\nunder the same theorem. Recheck the maximal-extension and norm\nexports.</p>"}, {"label": "Publication and reuse", "html": "<p>The corrected export retains its explicit assumptions. A hypothetical\nrevision receives a new version, and each consuming activity is\nrechecked; this scenario is not a recorded runtime event. <strong>Next\ndirection:</strong> Deduce that every nonzero vector has a norming\ncontinuous linear functional by first defining it on its one-dimensional\nspan.</p>"}], "references": "<p><a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-102-introduction-to-functional-analysis-spring-2021/resources/lecture-notes/\">MIT\nOpenCourseWare, Introduction to Functional Analysis: lecture notes</a>.\nSee the lectures on integration, Hilbert spaces, Baire category, and\nHahn–Banach.</p>", "sha256": "79bc0394e0e6a594e4738415155220d9fbd1d606d19829ee3a4b691c722a4c13", "pdf": "reports/pdf/hahn-banach-real-extension.pdf"}], "links": [{"source": "FA-02", "target": "FA-03", "label": "Hilbert Projection Theorem", "detail": "FA-03 explicitly imports FA-02 under the version and assumptions in its import contract."}], "evidence": "Authored proof walkthroughs relative to declared imports; no agent execution or formal verification claimed."};
